    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0629" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg315"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-28">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>See Department’s August 23, 6 p.m., to Ambassador and previous instructions to
                        you.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d480-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>If you deem advisable you may appear before Bonar Law’s committee for expeditious
                    settlement of matter of freight, making plain the attitude of this Government as
                    stated in instructions referred to, and in order to prevent losses from further
                    detention on account of payment of freight, you may advise American interests to
                    pay freight if finally demanded with protest, question to be determined on
                    principle later, and if decided in our favor all freight collected to be
                    reimbursed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
